  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 PM EDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\n- Clearing And Frost Tonight\n\nPost frontal dir air and associated high pressure has led to mainly \nsome diurnal stratocu, which will diminish tonight leading to clear \nskies. This will cause temps to fall as radiational cooling takes \nhold into the 30s across much of the area. Frost advisory looks good \nacross the interior counties of Central Lower Michigan. \nProbabilistic guidance suggests chances are low for temps to fall \nbelow freezing, but would not be surprised so see some of our cold \nhollows like Leota get that cold overnight.\n\n- Light Chance of Rain Sunday Morning, Then Frost/Freeze Possible\n\nA low chance of rain exists mainly north of M20 Sunday morning as a \nmid-level wave and associated moisture provide a glancing blow to \nour northern counties. A cold front crossing the area Sunday ends \nthe low rain chances and marks the arrival of a notably cooler \nairmass. 850mb temps fall to near 0C across our interior north. \nGiven light winds/high pressure/clear skies a favorable setup for \nfrost, potentially freeze conditions, will be in place Sunday night \nacross our northern two rows and Monday Night areawide. Otherwise, \nlook for highs in the 60s and mild dewpoints making for comfortable \nfall conditions.",
